meta {
  name: upload the bytes
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{uploadUrl}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: image/png
}

tests {
  test("S3 accepted the object", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Goes straight to S3, not to this API - file bytes never pass through it.

  Two things matter here. `Content-Type` has to match what the presign was
  asked for, because it is part of what was signed. And this request must not
  inherit the collection's auth, hence `auth: none`.

  Set the body to a file: **Body -> File**, and pick
  `bruno/fixtures/sample.png`. Bruno stores that path per machine, so it is
  not in the committed file.
}
